    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2785?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "PhD Student Position (f/m/x) in “Quantum",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nPhD Student Position (f/m/x) in “Quantum \nHall calorimetry of quantum materials“ \nOne PhD Student position is available in the group of  \nProfessor Erwann Bocquillon, which specializes in the \nquantum transport of quantum materials ( https://ph2.uni-\nkoeln.de/en/research-groups/bocquillon).\nYOUR TASKS\n » This PhD project will develop a new ultra-sensitive \nquantum calorimeter to explore how heat flows through \nexotic quantum materials. By combining layered crystals \nwith quantum Hall devices, the researcher will be able to \nprobe elusive states of matter with unprecedented pre-\ncision—starting with alpha-RuCl3, a leading candidate for \nhosting Majorana-like particles and a quantum spin liquid. \nThe project offers an opportunity to build new cutting-  \nedge techniques in collaboration with partners at the \nUniversity of Tokyo (Japan), while tackling some exciting \nopen questions in condensed-matter physics.\nYOUR PROFILE\n » The candidate should possess an excellent academic \nrecord and hold a Masters in Physics, preferably with  \na major in Quantum Physics or Condensed Matter  \nPhysics. Research experience in one or several of the \nfollowing fields will be appreciated: cryogenic systems, \nquantum transport measurements, nano-fabrication \nand cleanroom techniques\n » An excellent command of English, as well as high  \nmotivation, commitment, good communication skills \nand team spirit are expected.\nWE OFFER\n » An exciting research project at the forefront of research \non quantum matter\n » A diverse working environment with equal opportunities\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities\n » Occupational health management offers\n » Flexible working time models\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities \nand diversity. Women will be considered preferentially \nin accordance with the Equal Opportunities Act of North \nRhine-Westphalia (Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG \nNRW). We also expressly welcome applications from all \nsuitable candidates regardless of their gender, nationality, \nethnic and social origin, religion, disability, age, sexual \norientation and identity.\nThe position is available from 1 January 2027 on a part-\ntime basis (29,87 hours per week).The position is to \nbe filled for a fixed term until 31 December 2029. If the \napplicant meets the relevant wage requirements and \npersonal qualifications, the salary is based on remune -\nration group 13 TV-L of the pay scale for the German \npublic sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qualifications \nwithout a photo under: https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. \nThe reference number is Wiss2610-07. The application \ndeadline is 30 November 2026. \nFor further inquiries, please contact Professor Dr Erwann \nBocquillon (bocquillon@ph2.uni-koeln.de) (scientific part) \nor Dr Matteo Cacco ( cacco@ph2.uni-koeln.de) (applica-\ntion questions) and take a look at our FAQs. \nInstitute of Physics II |  Bocquillon Working Group\nFaculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences\n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2788?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "unserer Region. Durch unser breites Fächerspektrum, die dynamische Entwicklung unserer Forschungsschwerpunkte",
      "description": "Wir sind eine der größten und ältesten Universitäten Europas und gehören zu den größten Arbeitgeber*innen in  \nunserer Region. Durch unser breites Fächerspektrum, die dynamische Entwicklung unserer Forschungsschwerpunkte \nund unseren Standort mitten in Köln sind wir attraktiv für Studierende und Forschende weltweit. Wir bieten vielfältige \nKarrierechancen in Wissenschaft, Technik und Verwaltung.\nAm Institut für Mathematikdidaktik der Mathematisch-Natur-\nwissenschaftlichen Fakultät wird zum Lehren und Lernen \nvon Mathematik geforscht. Des Weiteren verantwortet das \nInstitut die Lehre in den Lehramtsstudiengängen Mathematik \nund ist an das Department Didaktiken der Mathematik und \nder Naturwissenschaften angegliedert.\nIHRE AUFGABEN\n » Entwicklung und Durchführung eines eigenen  \nPromotionsvorhabens in einem Bereich der Didaktik  \nder Mathematik\n » Erstellung wissenschaftlicher Publikationen in Form von \nZeitschriftenartikeln und Tagungsbeiträgen\n » Umsetzung und Durchführung von Lehrveranstaltungen \nim Umfang von 3 SWS in Mathematikdidaktik und/oder \nMathematik für die Lehramtsstudiengänge\n » Unterstützung in der akademischen Selbstverwaltung\nIHR PROFIL\n » abgeschlossenes wissenschaftliches Hochschulstudium \n(Master, Diplom, Magister oder Staatsexamen), vorzugs-\nweise im Lehramt Mathematik \n » starkes Interesse an der Durchführung empirischer  \nForschung im Bereich der Mathematikdidaktik\n » hohe Motivation und Bereitschaft, sich intensiv in ein \nPromotionsprojekt einzuarbeiten\n » Neugier und Offenheit für neue Forschungsideen und \nmethodische Ansätze\n » hohe Teamfähigkeit, selbstständiges Arbeiten\nWIR BIETEN IHNEN\n » ein engagiertes Team, in dem großer Wert auf eine  \nproduktive und kollaborative Atmosphäre gelegt wird\n » ein vielfältiges und chancengerechtes Arbeitsumfeld \n » Unterstützung bei der Vereinbarkeit von Beruf und  \nFamilie \n » flexible Arbeitszeitmodelle\n » ein umfangreiches Weiterbildungsangebot \n » Angebote im Rahmen des Betrieblichen Gesundheits-\nmanagements \n » Möglichkeit zur mobilen Arbeit \nDie Universität zu Köln fördert Chancengerechtigkeit und \nVielfalt. Bewerbungen von Frauen werden nach Maßgabe \ndes LGG NRW bevorzugt berücksichtigt. Wir begrüßen aus-\ndrücklich alle Bewerbungen – unabhängig von Geschlecht, \nNationalität, ethnischer und sozialer Herkunft, Religion, \nBehinderung, Alter sowie sexueller Orientierung und Identität.\nDie Stellen sind ab sofort in Teilzeit (29,87 Wochen -\nstunden) zu besetzen. Sie sind auf 2 Jahre befristet mit \nder Option einer Verlängerung um 1 Jahr. Sofern die \nentsprechenden tariflichen und persönlichen Voraus -\nsetzungen vorliegen, richtet sich die Vergütung nach der \nEntgeltgruppe 13 TV-L.\nBitte bewerben Sie sich mit Ihren aussagekräftigen \nBewerbungsunterlagen inkl. beigefügten Nachweisen für \ndie gesuchten Qualifikationen ohne Bewerbungsfoto online \nunter: https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. \nDie Kennziffer ist Wiss2610-09. Die Bewerbungsfrist endet \nam 22.11.2026.\nBei Fragen wenden Sie sich bitte an Herrn Prof. Dr. Benjamin \nRott (brott@uni-koeln.de) und schauen Sie in unsere FAQs.\n2 Wissenschaftliche Mitarbeiter*innen (w/m/d)\nInstitut für Mathematikdidaktik\nMathematisch-Naturwissenschaftliche Fakultät\n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2796?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nFloodplains are dynamic, valuable ecosystems increasingly threatened by river \nregulation, land use, and climate change. The University of Cologne’s project \n“The Rhine Floodplain – a Biogeochemically Coupled System under Stress” \ninvestigates how altered hydrology affects sediment dynamics, biodiversity, \nfood webs, microbial processes, and greenhouse gas emissions.\nYOUR TASKS\n » Develop a mechanistic framework linking hydrological drivers to biotic, \nsedimentary and biogeochemical floodplain processes\n » Derive inundation and connectivity metrics from water-level and sedi-\nmentary records as well as an existing hydronumeric model\n » Assess aquatic and terrestrial habitat availability under past and projected \nwater levels\n » Lead concept-driven synthesis of floodplain functioning in an interdisci-\nplinary network of bio- and geoscientists\n » Coordinate the project, joint sampling design and field campaigns\n » Publish as lead author and contribute to a planned Collaborative Re-\nsearch Centre\n » Co-supervise students and co-organise an international summer school\nYOUR PROFILE\n » PhD in hydrology, physical geography, geosciences, ecology or a related \nfield\n » Strong publication record appropriate to career stage\n » Strong skills in hydrological data analysis (R or Python) and GIS-based \nspatial analysis\n » Experience with hydronumeric modelling and/or habitat suitability mo-\ndelling\n » Interest in linking physical drivers with ecological and biogeochemical \nprocesses\n » Experience in fieldwork\n » Experience in coordinating collaborative research is desirable\n » Excellent scientific writing and communication skills in English (C1 equi-\nvalent) are essential, some knowledge of German is beneficial\nWE OFFER\n » Exciting research in an interdisciplinary project with several PhD students\n » A diverse working environment with equal opportunities\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Flexible working time models\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities\n » Occupational health management offers\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities and diversity. Women \nwill be considered preferentially in accordance with the Equal Opportunities \nAct of North Rhine-Westphalia (Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG NRW). We \nalso expressly welcome applications from all suitable candidates regardless of \ntheir gender, nationality, ethnic and social origin, religion, disability, age, sexual \norientation and identity.\nThe position is available from 1 February 2027 on a full time basis with \n39,83 hours per week. The position is to be filled for a fixed term until \n31 January 2030. If the applicant meets the relevant wage requirements \nand has the appropriate personal qualifications, the salary is based on \nremuneration group 13 TV-L of the pay scale for the German public sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qualifications (without a photo) \nunder https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. The reference number is Wiss2611-01. \nThe application deadline is 4 December 2026.\nFor further inquiries, please contact Professor Dr Patrick Fink at   \n(patrick.fink@uni-koeln.de) and take a look at our FAQs. \nPostdoctoral scientist in interdisciplinary floodplain research (f/m/x)\nFaculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences\nInstitute of Zoology, General Ecology research group\n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2800?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "unserer Region. Durch unser breites Fächerspektrum, die dynamische Entwicklung unserer Forschungsschwerpunkte",
      "description": "Wir sind eine der größten und ältesten Universitäten Europas und gehören zu den größten Arbeitgeber*innen in  \nunserer Region. Durch unser breites Fächerspektrum, die dynamische Entwicklung unserer Forschungsschwerpunkte \nund unseren Standort mitten in Köln sind wir attraktiv für Studierende und Forschende weltweit. Wir bieten vielfältige \nKarrierechancen in Wissenschaft, Technik und Verwaltung.\nWie lassen sich individuelle und kollektive Selbstbestimmung in der postdigitalen Gesell -\nschaft fördern? Und welche Bedeutung haben dabei Konzepte wie Aufklärung, Mündigkeit \nund Souveränität? Mit diesen Fragen beschäftigt sich das von der Fritz Thyssen Stiftung \ngeförderte Forschungsprojekt „Digitale Selbstbestimmung“. \nDas Projekt verbindet Perspektiven aus Medienwissenschaft, Rechtswissenschaft und \nMedienökonomie. Es untersucht, wie digitale Selbstbestimmung in wissenschaftlichen \nund öffentlichen Diskursen verhandelt wird, welche Gemeinsamkeiten und Unterschiede \nzwischen fachlichen Zugängen bestehen und wie daraus neue wissenschaftliche und \ngesellschaftliche Handlungsmöglichkeiten entwickelt werden können.\nIHRE AUFGABEN\n » eigenständige Mitarbeit im Forschungsprojekt, insbesondere bei der Untersuchung \nund Rekonstruktion von Begriffen und Modellen digitaler Selbstbestimmung\n » Mitarbeit an der Analyse von öffentlichen und disziplinären Diskursen über (post)\ndigitale Aufklärung, Mündigkeit und Souveränität sowie ihrer transdisziplinären Ein-\nordnung\n » Redaktionelle und konzeptionelle Weiterentwicklung des Glossars zur digitalen \nSelbstbestimmung sowie Aufbereitung und Veröffentlichung von Forschungsergeb-\nnissen\n » Konzeption, Organisation und Begleitung von Workshops und wissenschaftlichen \nVeranstaltungen\n » Mitwirkung an der Wissenschaftskommunikation und öffentlichen Vermittlung der \nProjektergebnisse\nIHR PROFIL\n » Ageschlossenes Hochschulstudium in einem der drei beteiligten Fächer: Rechtswis-\nsenschaft, Volkswirtschaftslehre oder einem medienkulturwissenschaftlichen Fach\n » Interesse an Fragen digitaler Selbstbestimmung sowie an den gesellschaftlichen, \nrechtlichen, kulturellen und ökonomischen Bedingungen digitaler Medien und Infra-\nstrukturen\n » Sehr gute schriftliche und mündliche Kommunikationsfähigkeiten sowie die Fähigkeit, \nwissenschaftliche Inhalte für unterschiedliche fachliche und öffentliche Zielgruppen \naufzubereiten\n » Organisationsfähigkeit und die Bereitschaft, wissenschaftliche Zusammenarbeit, Ver-\nanstaltungen und Publikationsprozesse eigenständig zu koordinieren\n » Wünschenswert sind darüber hinaus: eine abgeschlossene Promotion; Kenntnisse \nund Erfahrungen in mindestens einem der jeweils anderen beiden Fachbereiche \n(Medienkulturwissenschaft, Rechtswissenschaft oder Volkswirtschaftslehre); Er-\nfahrungen in der transdisziplinären oder interdisziplinären Forschungskoordination \nund Zusammenarbeit; Erfahrungen mit diskursanalytischen Forschungsansätzen, der \nredaktionellen Arbeit an wissenschaftlichen Publikationen oder der Wissenschafts-\nkommunikation\nWIR BIETEN IHNEN\n » Die Mitarbeit in einem transdisziplinären Forschungsprojekt\n » Ein vielfältiges und chancengerechtes Arbeitsumfeld\n » Unterstützung bei der Vereinbarkeit von Beruf und Familie \n » Flexible Arbeitszeitmodelle, teilbare Vollzeitstelle\n » Umfangreiches Weiterbildungsangebot \n » Angebote im Rahmen des Betrieblichen Gesundheitsmanagements \n » Möglichkeit zur mobilen Arbeit\nDie Universität zu Köln fördert Chancengerechtigkeit und Vielfalt. Bewerbungen von Frauen \nwerden nach Maßgabe des LGG NRW bevorzugt berücksichtigt. Wir begrüßen ausdrücklich \nalle Bewerbungen – unabhängig von Geschlecht, Nationalität, ethnischer und sozialer Her-\nkunft, Religion, Behinderung, Alter sowie sexueller Orientierung und Identität.\nDie Stelle ist ab 01.02.2027 in Vollzeit (39,83 Wochenstunden) zu besetzen. Die \nStelle kann auf Wunsch auch geteilt und dann in Teilzeit mit 50 v.H. der regelmäßigen \nArbeitszeit besetzt werden; bitte geben Sie in Ihrer Bewerbung Ihre Präferenz an. \nSie ist bis zum 30.09.2028 befristet. Sofern die entsprechenden tariflichen und persön-\nlichen Voraussetzungen vorliegen, richtet sich die Vergütung nach der Entgeltgruppe \n13 TV-L.\nBitte bewerben Sie sich mit Ihren aussagekräftigen Bewerbungsunteragen inkl. beigefügten \nNachweisen für die gesuchten Qualifikationen ohne Bewerbungsfoto online  unter:  \nhttps://jobportal.uni-koeln.de.  \nDie Kennziffer ist Wiss2611-04.  Die Bewerbungsfrist endet am 10.12.2026.. \nBei Fragen wenden Sie sich bitte an Prof. Dr. Stephan Packard (packard@uni-koeln.de) und \nschauen Sie in unsere FAQs.\nWissenschaftliche Mitarbeiterin (w/m/d)\nPhilosophische Fakultät\nfür Forschung und transdisziplinäre Koordination im Projekt „Digitale Selbstbestimmung“\n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2802?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nFloodplains are dynamic, valuable ecosystems increasingly threate-\nned by river regulation, land use, and climate change. The University \nof Cologne’s project “The Rhine Floodplain – a Biogeochemically \nCoupled System under Stress” investigates how altered hydrology \naffects sediment dynamics, biodiversity, food webs, microbial pro -\ncesses, and greenhouse gas emissions.\nYOUR TASKS\n » Characterise floodplain sediments using sedimentological and \ngeochemical techniques\n » Determine deposition ages and sedimentation rates using lumi-\nnescence dating and fallout radionuclides\n » Quantify microplastics and heavy metals in floodplain sediments\n » Quantify bioturbation using luminescence-based methods, \nearthworm surveys and laboratory experiments\n » Collaborate in joint field campaigns with an interdisciplinary \nteam\nYOUR PROFILE\n » MSc in geography, geosciences, soil science, biology or a rela-\nted field\n » Experience in laboratory work and the analysis of complex data-\nsets\n » Ability and willingness to undertake fieldwork, including exten-\nded stays at the Ecological Research Station Rees\n » Experience in sedimentological or geochemical analysis, lumi-\nnescence dating or microplastic analysis is desirable\n » Excellent communication skills in English (C1 equivalent)\n » Proficiency in German is desirable\nWE OFFER\n » Exciting research in an interdisciplinary project with 2 other PhD \nstudents and a postdoc\n » A diverse working environment with equal opportunities\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Flexible working time models\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities\n » Occupational health management offers\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities and \ndiversity. Women will be considered preferentially in accordance \nwith the Equal Opportunities Act of North Rhine-Westphalia \n(Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG NRW). We also expressly wel -\ncome applications from all suitable candidates regardless of their \ngender, nationality, ethnic and social origin, religion, disability, age, \nsexual orientation and identity.\nThe position is available from 1 February 2027 on a part time basis \nwith 25,89 hours per week. The position is to be filled for a fixed \nterm until 31 January 2030. If the applicant meets the relevant \nwage requirements and has the appropriate personal qualifica -\ntions, the salary is based on remuneration group 13 TV-L of the \npay scale for the German public sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qualifications (without \na photo) under https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. The reference number \nis Wiss2611-06. \nThe application deadline is 10 December 2026.\nFor further inquiries, please contact Junior Professor Dr Svenja Rie-\ndesel at  (svenja.riedesel@uni-koeln.de) and take a look at our FAQs. \nInterdisciplinary PhD position (f/m/x)\nFaculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences\nThe Rhine Floodplain – a Biogeochemically Coupled System under Stress \n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2801?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "compact Poisson manifold” (PI: Professor Dr Ioan Mărcuț).",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nPostdoctoral position (f/m/x) for two years, funded by the \nDFG grant “The universal deformation space of a source-\ncompact Poisson manifold” (PI: Professor Dr Ioan Mărcuț). \n(https://gepris.dfg.de/project/580538076?lang=en)\nYOUR TASKS\n » Conduct research within the framework of the project\n » Participate in the seminars, workshops, and other \nresearch activities of the Poisson Geometry group in \nCologne\n » There are no teaching obligations\n » There will be opportunities to organize research and \nlearning seminars and to get involved in teaching\nYOUR PROFILE\n » A PhD in mathematics, obtained or to be obtained  \nby 1 February 2027 at the latest\n » Research experience in an area closely related to  \nthe DFG project, specifically Poisson geometry,  \nLie algebroids and groupoids, or deformation theory  \nof geometric structures\n » Enthusiasm for collaborating with members of the  \nPoisson Geometry group in Cologne\n » An interest in learning new topics and communicating \nthem to fellow researchers\nWE OFFER\n » A diverse working environment with equal opportunities\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities\n » Occupational health management offers\n » Flexible working time models\n » Opportunity to work remotely\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities and \ndiversity. Women will be considered preferentially in accor -\ndance with the Equal Opportunities Act of North Rhine-\nWestphalia (Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG NRW). \nWe also expressly welcome applications from all suitable \ncandidates regardless of their gender, nationality, ethnic and \nsocial origin, religion, disability, age, sexual orientation and \nidentity.\nThe position is available from 1 April 2027 on a full-time \nbasis (39,83 hours per week). The position is to be filled \nfor a fixed term until 31 March 2029. If the applicant meets \nthe relevant wage requirements and personal qualifica -\ntions, the salary is based on remuneration group 13 TV-L \nof the pay scale for the German public sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qualifications \nwithout a photo under: https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. \nThe reference number is Wiss2611-08. The application dead-\nline is 13 December 2026. \nRequired documents: CV (including publication list, and the \nemail addresses of two people who are willing to recom -\nmend you for the position; in case of ongoing PhD, one of \nthese references should be the PhD advisor), cover letter, \nresearch statement.  \nFor further inquiries, please contact Professor Dr Ioan Marcut \n(imarcut@uni-koeln.de) and take a look at our FAQs. \nPostdoctoral position (f/m/x) in Poisson Geometry\nFaculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences\nDepartment of Mathematics and Computer Science  | Division of Mathematics \n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2803?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "food webs, microbial processes, and greenhouse gas emissions. The position",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nFloodplains are dynamic, valuable ecosystems increasingly threatened by river \nregulation, land use, and climate change. The University of Cologne’s project \n“The Rhine Floodplain – a Biogeochemically Coupled System under Stress” \ninvestigates how altered hydrology affects sediment dynamics, biodiversity, \nfood webs, microbial processes, and greenhouse gas emissions. The position \nis co-supervised between the University of Cologne and Forschungszentrum \nJülich.\nYOUR TASKS\n » Conduct field measurements of greenhouse gas and VOC (volatile orga-\nnic compounds) emissions along hydrological gradients in the floodplain\n » Perform laboratory measurements of VOC samples using thermal de-\nsorption gas chromatography coupled with mass spectrometry (TD-GC-\nMS)\n » Carry out nutrient addition experiments (C, N, P) to assess microbial \nnutrient limitation and its effects on microbial biomass, respiration, car-\nbon-use efficiency, and enzyme allocation\n » Integrate microbial stoichiometric responses with gas flux data to identify \nhow nutrient constraints regulate carbon partitioning and climate-re-\nlevant emissions\n » Collaborate within an interdisciplinary team spanning biology, geoscien-\nces and atmospheric science.\n » Present your research results at international conferences and publish \nthem in peer-reviewed journals\nYOUR PROFILE\n » Master‘s degree in Environmental Sciences, Biogeochemistry or a related \nfield; experience with using analytical chemistry instrumentation (GC-\nMS) is desired\n » Excellent experimental skills\n » Knowledge of statistics and programming\n » Excellent written and oral presentation and communication skills in Eng-\nlish (C1 equivalent)\n » Driving experience and driving licence for cars\n » Ability to work independently in the field\n » Self-motivated and structured working style\n » Working and living at the field station, work at the University of Cologne \nand forschungszentrum Jülich requires a high amount of flexibility\nWE OFFER\n » Exciting research in an interdisciplinary project with 2 other PhD students \nand a postdoc\n » A diverse working environment with equal opportunities\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Flexible working time models\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities\n » Occupational health management offers\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities and diversity. Women \nwill be considered preferentially in accordance with the Equal Opportunities \nAct of North Rhine-Westphalia (Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG NRW). We \nalso expressly welcome applications from all suitable candidates regardless of \ntheir gender, nationality, ethnic and social origin, religion, disability, age, sexual \norientation and identity.\nThe position is available from 1 February 2027 on a part time basis with \n25,89 hours per week. The position is to be filled for a fixed term until \n31 January 2030. If the applicant meets the relevant wage requirements \nand has the appropriate personal qualifications, the salary is based on \nremuneration group 13 TV-L of the pay scale for the German public sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qualifications (without a photo) \nunder https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. The reference number is Wiss2611-05. \nThe application deadline is 15 December 2026.\nFor further inquiries, please contact Professor Dr Eva Pfannerstill \n( epfanner@uni-koeln.de) or Professor Michael Bonkowski \n(m.bonkowski@uni-koeln.de) and take a look at our FAQs. \nPhD position in Biogeochemistry/Soil Biology (f/m/x)\nFaculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences\nSoil microbial nutrient stoichiometry and soil-atmosphere exchange in river floodplains\n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2804?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "position for a Research Associate is available.",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nAs part of the German Research Founda -\ntion (DFG) funded long-term research pro -\nject “The Setsuyôshû Dictionary” (for details, see  \nhttps://gepris.dfg.de/project/580044654/2?lang=en), a \nposition for a Research Associate is available.\nYOUR TASKS\n » Transcription of Edo-period dictionaries (i.e. setsuyôs-\nhû)\n » Translation into German and English with critical an-\nnotation \n » Development of a comprehensive commentary and \nsubject apparatus \n » Review, validation, and quality assurance of data sets \nfor the digital online dictionary \n » Active involvement in the project‘s outreach activities\nYOUR PROFILE\n » M.A. degree in Japanese Studies with a focus on the \npre-modern period\n » Solid expertise in the transcription of pre-modern \nwoodblock prints\n » Excellent knowledge of both modern and classical \nJapanese\n » Excellent command of English\n » Proven experience in academic research environments\n » Proficiency in Microsoft and Adobe software applicati-\nons\n » Basic knowledge of database management\nWE OFFER\n » Opportunity to pursue a Ph.D. degree\n » A diverse working environment with equal opportuni-\nties\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities\n » Occupational health management offers\n » Flexible working time models\n » Opportunity to work remotely\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities \nand diversity. Women will be considered preferentially \nin accordance with the Equal Opportunities Act of North \nRhine-Westphalia (Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG \nNRW). We also expressly welcome applications from all \nsuitable candidates regardless of their gender, nationality, \nethnic and social origin, religion, disability, age, sexual \norientation and identity.\nThe position is available from 1 April 2027 on a part-time \nbasis (29,87 hours per week). It is limited for a fixed term \nuntil 31 March 2030. If the applicant meets the relevant \nwage requirements and personal qualifications, the \nsalary is based on remuneration group 13 TV-L of the \npay scale for the German public sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qua -\nlifications without photo under: https://jobportal.\nuni-koeln.de. The reference number is 2611-07. The \napplication deadline is 12 December 2026. For further \ninquiries, please contact Professor Dr Stephan Koehn  \n(stephan.koehn@uni-koeln.de) and take a look at our FAQs. \nResearch Associate (f/m/x)\nFaculty of Arts and Humanities\nInstitute of Japanese Studies\n"
    },
    "https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de/ausschreibung/renderFile/2786?propertyName=flyer": {
      "title": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.",
      "description": "We are one of the largest and oldest universities in Europe and one of the most important employers in our region.  \nOur broad range of subjects, the dynamic development of our main research areas and our central location in Cologne \nmake us attractive for students and researchers from around the world. We offer a wide range of career opportunities in \nscience, technology, and administration.\nPhD position (f/m/x) in  \npaleoecology of Antarctic lakes\nThe position is funded by the DFG under the Priority Pro -\ngramme SPP 1158 Antarctic Research. Within the framework \nof the project, you will investigate the palaeoecological evo-\nlution of lakes in East Antarctica. The focus is on how micro-\nbial communities in Antarctic lakes have evolved during the \nHolocene in response to changes in the environment and \nclimate. You will study sediment deposits from various lakes \nand reconstruct their environmental and ecosystem evolu -\ntion over time. A key focus of your work is the comprehensive \nanalysis of lipid biomarkers and their interpretation within the \ncontext of the palaeoecology of the lakes. In addition, further \nparameters derived from micro- and macro-palaeontologi -\ncal, sedimentological and isotopic geochemical observations \nare recorded and incorporated into the interpretation.\nYOUR TASKS\n » The planning, implementation, and evaluation of labora-\ntory and analytical work on Antarctic sediment samples \nusing GC-MS and HPLC-UV-Vis spectrophotometry, \nEA-IRMS, and microscopic techniques\n » The integration of findings from these geochemical, \nisotopic and sedimentological investigations to gain a \nbetter understanding of limnic systems with regard to \nthe interaction between the environment and ecology \n » The presentation of results at national and international \nconferences and the publication of research findings in \ninternational specialist journals\n » Collaboration within an interdisciplinary and international \nresearch environment\nYOUR PROFILE\n » You hold a postgraduate degree (M.Sc. or equivalent) \nin a subject area relevant to the project, such as earth \nsciences, environmental sciences or a related discipline.\n » You have a sound background in at least one area  \nrelevant to the project and are keen to familiarise \nyourself with further methods and research questions. \nExperience in organic geochemistry, biomarker analysis \n(e.g. GC-MS, HPLC-MS), microscopy and sedimentology \nis particularly welcome.\nIn addition, we expect:\n » Motivation to work in an interdisciplinary and  \ninternational research environment \n » A willingness and interest in collaborating with  \nresearchers both within and outside the project  \nand in establishing new scientific partnerships \n » Good communication and teamwork skills \n » Excellent written and spoken English\nWE OFFER\n » Working in an internationally well-established research \ngroup with the opportunity to obtain a Ph.D. degree \n » A diverse working environment with equal opportunities\n » Support in balancing work and family life\n » Extensive advanced training opportunities, e.g. within  \nthe GSGS graduate school of the department of  \nGeosciences\n » Occupational health management offers\n » Flexible working time models\nThe University of Cologne promotes equal opportunities and \ndiversity. Women will be considered preferentially in accord-\nance with the Equal Opportunities Act of North Rhine-West-\nphalia (Landesgleichstellungsgesetz – LGG NRW). We also \nexpressly welcome applications from all suitable candidates \nregardless of their gender, nationality, ethnic and social \norigin, religion, disability, age, sexual orientation and identity.\nThe position is available from 1 January 2027 on a part-\ntime basis (29,87 hours per week). The position is to be \nfilled for a fixed term for 3 years. If the applicant meets the \nrelevant wage requirements and personal qualifications, \nthe salary is based on remuneration group 13 TV-L of the \npay scale for the German public sector.\nPlease apply online with proof of the required qualifications \nwithout a photo under: https://jobportal.uni-koeln.de. \nThe reference number is Wiss2611-09. The application dead-\nline is 15 December 2026. \nFor further inquiries, please contact Dr Sonja Berg  \n(sonja.berg@uni-koeln.de) or Professor Dr Christine Heim \n(christine.heim@uni-koeln.de) and take a look at our FAQs. \nInstitute of Geology and Mineralogy |  Geobiology\nFaculty of Mathematics and Natural Sciences\n"
    }
  },
